ary strategies  and thinking he can seduce any woman he  pleases  in the 1999 episode Love's Labour's Lost  in Space Zapp tries to seduce Leela by  laying in bed in his robe with his  paunch clearly visible inside the outfit  behind him on the wall  what appears to be his official  captain's portrait his arms are crossed  and his head bowed as if deep in  thoughts which seems to suggest the  soulful thoughtful leader of men he's  none of those things of course which is  why it's hilarious it's also an exact  recreation of a famous painting Aaron  sheckler's official presidential  portrait of John F Kennedy Zapp would  compare himself to a revered politician  wouldn't he in the 2001 episode Roswell  that ends well  prime microwaves a metal popcorn  container on the Planet Express ship  rise mistake upsets the balance of  radiation and sends the ship back  through time in space  crash landing the crew in Roswell New  Mexico in 1947 to return to the future  Professor Farnsworth needs microwave  technology of some kind and the  microwave antenna at the local military  base would work he warns bride that  acquiring it could be tricky as fries  grandfather  eNOS works at that base and if he killed  him he'd erases existence fry tries to  protect his grandfather as best he can  and to prevent harm he locks him in a  house which she doesn't realize is  located on a nuclear weapon testing  range the test kills eNOS almost  immediately and Pryde tries to comfort  eNOS as fiance a diner waitress named  Mildred but they wind up sleeping  together probably figures that since he  didn't blink out of existence when eNOS  died then eNOS must not have been his  grandfather as it turns out Mildred is  still his grandmother she just became  pregnant by pride as Professor  Farnsworth tells fry oh lesson in not  changing history from mr. I'm my own  grandpa let's get the hell out of here  already  screw history Farnsworth's mockery is  actually an explicit reference to I'm my  own grand